      "text": "To solve for the \\(x\\)-values that satisfy the equation \\(5 = \\frac{x^3 - 2x^2 - 8x}{x + 2}\\), we start by simplifying the right-hand side of the equation. We'll do this by polynomial long division and checking if there are any common factors.\n\n1. **Simplify the Fraction**: Start by performing polynomial long division on \\(x^3 - 2x^2 - 8x\\) by \\(x + 2\\):\n\nWhen dividing \\(x^3 - 2x^2 - 8x\\) by \\(x + 2\\), we guide:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{rrrrrrrr}\n& & & x^2 & -4x & + 8 & \\\\\nx + 2 & | & x^3 + 0x^2 - 2x^2 - 8x & \\\\\n& & - (x^3 + 2x^2) \\\\\n& & & -4x^2 & - 8x \\\\\n& & & - (-4x^2 - 8x) \\\\\n& & & & 0x^2 & + 0x \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\nSince \\(x^3 + 2x^2\\) cancels out remaining: \n\\[\nx^3 - 2x^2 - 8x\n\\)\nHaving terms: \\(-8x\\)\nThe division simplifies giving:\n\\[\n\\frac{x^3 - 2x^2 - 8x}{x + 2} = x^2 - 4x + 8\n\\]\nThus variable simplification to solve:\n\\[\n5 = x^2 - 4x + 8\n\\]\n\n2. **Solve the equation \\(!x! - 4x + 8):**\n\n\\[\n5 = x^2 - 4x + 8\n\\]\nRewriting with zero on the right-hand side:\n\\[\nx^2 - 4x + 8 - 5 = 0 \\implies x^2 - 4x + 3 = 0\n\\]\nUsing the quadratic formula \\(x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\) for \\(a = 1\\), \\(b = -4\\), and \\(c = 3\\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-(-4) \\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 3}}{2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{4 \\pm \\sqrt{16 - 12}}{2} = \\frac{4 \\pm \\sqrt{4}}{2} = \\frac{4 \\pm 2}{2}\n\\]\n\nSolve the two possible \\(x\\)-values:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{4 + 2}{2} = 3,\\quad x = \\frac{4 - 2}{2} = 1\n\\]\n\n3. **Sum the confirmed solutions**: \n\nWe are provided with the solutions previously \nUsing mathematical notation separate the solutions individually:\n\\[\nx_1 = x_2 = 1\\quad +\\quad x_3 = 3 \n\\]\n\nOur binary sum of all three solutions combined:\n\\boxed{5}\n\nSum mounted \\( desired\\ \\( three \\) \\( total \\) \\( values \\boxed{5}\\)",
